<h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="tagline">What we collect, why, and who we share it with.</p>

<section class="card">
  <div class="content">
    <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: 5 October 2026</p>
    <p>
      This policy explains what personal information we collect, why, and what we do with it. We keep it to the minimum we need to run this website, sell you a licence and support you.
    </p>
    <p>
      &ldquo;We&rdquo; means Daniel Hampton, a sole trader in Queensland, Australia, trading under the registered business name Practical Supply Chain Planning, ABN 56 757 743 802. Contact: <a class="support-email" href="mailto:support@practicalsupplychainplanning.com">support@practicalsupplychainplanning.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>We follow the Australian Privacy Principles in the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth).</p>

    <h2>1. What we don&rsquo;t collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your planning data.</strong> Your stock, sales, forecast, supplier and order data stay on your PC. The app never sends them to us.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage tracking.</strong> The app doesn&rsquo;t send usage analytics or telemetry.</li>
      <li><strong>Card details.</strong> Paddle handles payment. We never see or store your card number.</li>
      <li><strong>Website tracking.</strong> Our website has no analytics, advertising or tracking cookies.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. When you use our free tools or sign up for articles</h2>
    <p>
      If you ask a page on this website to email you the results, we send one email to the address you typed. We keep a record of that request for 24 months: your email address, the time, the network address, which page you used, the wording you agreed to, and whether you also asked for new articles. We do not keep your SKU names, forecasts, prices, stock levels, or the result numbers. If you tick the articles box, we add your address to the Articles list. You can unsubscribe at any time. If a message bounces, or you unsubscribe, we keep the address on a do-not-email list so we do not write to you again. Questions:
      <a class="support-email" href="mailto:support@practicalsupplychainplanning.com">support@practicalsupplychainplanning.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you use Let's keep in touch, we add your email address to that same Articles list and keep a record of the request, including whether you ticked I'd be happy to beta test. We keep a beta tick until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it. A keep-in-touch request without a beta tick is deleted after 24 months.
    </p>

    <h2>3. When you start a trial or buy Practical Stock Planner</h2>
    <h3>From Paddle</h3>
    <p>Paddle is our reseller and Merchant of Record. When you start a trial or buy, Paddle tells us:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your name and email address;</li>
      <li>your Paddle customer ID and subscription ID;</li>
      <li>your subscription status (for example trialing, active, cancelled, payment failed) and billing dates;</li>
      <li>refund and chargeback events for your subscription.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Paddle also holds your payment, address and tax details. It uses them under its own <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">privacy notice</a>.
    </p>
    <h3>Your licence (on our licence server)</h3>
    <p>We store:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your name, email address and a customer code we create;</li>
      <li>your Paddle customer and subscription IDs;</li>
      <li>your licence key, licence status and expiry date;</li>
      <li>short notes about your licence (for example &ldquo;refunded&rdquo; or &ldquo;chargeback&rdquo;);</li>
      <li>the dates we sent you the emails listed below.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>When you activate and use the app</h3>
    <p>Each time the app activates or checks its licence (about once a week), our server records:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>a random installation ID and token created for that PC (not your PC&rsquo;s name, serial number or hardware details);</li>
      <li>the app version;</li>
      <li>when the installation was activated, last checked and (if moved) deactivated.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The app also keeps a small licence file on your PC, holding your installation token, your name and customer code, and the licence expiry date. It does not keep your licence key after activation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our hosting provider (Railway) may keep short-term technical logs of requests, which can include IP addresses.
    </p>

    <h2>4. When you contact us</h2>
    <p>
      If you email or leave a voicemail, we keep your message, your email address or phone number, and our reply, so we can help you. Voicemails are recorded by our phone provider and sent to our support inbox as an audio file.
    </p>

    <h2>5. When you visit our website</h2>
    <p>
      Our website is hosted by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical information such as your IP address and browser type to deliver pages and protect the site from attacks. The Practical Stock Planner page loads Paddle&rsquo;s checkout script (Paddle.js). Paddle may use cookies and device information for the checkout and to prevent fraud.
    </p>

    <h2>6. How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To send the results or articles you asked for.</li>
      <li>To send your licence key and make sure your licence works.</li>
      <li>To keep your licence in step with your subscription: trial, renewals, cancellations, failed payments, refunds.</li>
      <li>To stop licence sharing and misuse.</li>
      <li>To answer your questions.</li>
      <li>To ask for your feedback (see below) and improve the software.</li>
      <li>To meet our legal obligations (for example tax and record-keeping).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don&rsquo;t sell your information. We don&rsquo;t use it for advertising.</p>
    <h3>Emails we send to customers</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your licence key.</strong> Sent from <a class="support-email" href="mailto:support@practicalsupplychainplanning.com">support@practicalsupplychainplanning.com</a> straight after checkout. It includes your key, the download link and how to activate.</li>
      <li><strong>A one-question check-in</strong>, about a week after you start, sent once, from Daniel Hampton (<a class="support-email" href="mailto:daniel@practicalsupplychainplanning.com">daniel@practicalsupplychainplanning.com</a>).</li>
      <li><strong>A one-question &ldquo;what made you stop?&rdquo; email</strong> if you cancel or get a refund, sent once, from Daniel Hampton (<a class="support-email" href="mailto:daniel@practicalsupplychainplanning.com">daniel@practicalsupplychainplanning.com</a>). Not sent after a chargeback.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Replies to any of these go to <a class="support-email" href="mailto:support@practicalsupplychainplanning.com">support@practicalsupplychainplanning.com</a>. These emails are about your subscription. They contain no offers. If you&rsquo;d rather not get the feedback emails, reply &ldquo;stop&rdquo; and we won&rsquo;t email you again.
    </p>
    <p>Paddle also emails you receipts and subscription notices (including trial reminders). Those come from Paddle.</p>
    <p>We don&rsquo;t send marketing emails unless you&rsquo;ve agreed to receive them (for example by ticking the articles box).</p>

