    <p>
      Records of free-tool email requests, the Articles list and the do-not-email list are stored in Cloudflare D1.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some of these providers store information outside Australia, including the United States, Japan, the UK and Europe. We choose providers with good security practices and only share what&rsquo;s needed.
    </p>
    <p>We may also share information if the law requires it.</p>

    <h2>8. How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Free-tool email requests: 24 months.</li>
      <li>Articles list: until you unsubscribe. Do-not-email list: kept so we don&rsquo;t write to you again.</li>
      <li>Licence and customer records: while you&rsquo;re a customer and for 7 years after, for tax, record-keeping and disputes.</li>
      <li>Support emails and voicemails: 2 years.</li>
      <li>After that we delete it or make it anonymous.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Keeping it safe</h2>
    <p>
      Our licence server can only be managed by us, behind a password and a secret key. We never store card details. Connections to our website, licence server and email services are encrypted (HTTPS/TLS).
    </p>

    <h2>10. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask us to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>show you the personal information we hold about you;</li>
      <li>correct it;</li>
      <li>delete it. We may need to keep some records for legal reasons, and deleting your licence record will stop the software working.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Email <a class="support-email" href="mailto:support@practicalsupplychainplanning.com">support@practicalsupplychainplanning.com</a>. We&rsquo;ll reply within 30 days.
    </p>
    <p>
      For payment information held by Paddle, contact Paddle through <a href="https://www.paddle.net" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">paddle.net</a> or <a class="support-email" href="mailto:help@paddle.com">help@paddle.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you&rsquo;re unhappy with how we&rsquo;ve handled your information, please tell us first. You can also complain to the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (<a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">oaic.gov.au</a>), or to the data protection authority in your country.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We&rsquo;ll update this page if anything changes, and change the date at the top. If a change matters to you, we&rsquo;ll email you.
    </p>

